IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc7-12zc`

-- Tests for Part 12ZC (ss 171ZU-171ZZ5).  Every expected value is written beside its assertion from the
-- text of the Act (src:3718-4016), before the run, and is never copied from the code's output.
-- Figures that regulations or other Acts supply (the lower earnings limit, the prescribed rate, the prescribed
-- lengths and numbers of weeks) are ARBITRARY TEST INPUTS here, not law.
-- Calendar facts used: 1 January 2026 is a Thursday, so 4 January 2026 is a Sunday and 10 January a Saturday.

§ `Tests for Part 12ZC`

§§ `Fixtures`

`s 171ZU test person` MEANS Person WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1990
    `sex` IS Woman
    `marital status` IS `married`
    `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 1 1 2057

GIVEN began IS A DATE
      ended IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH AN Employment
`s 171ZU test employment` MEANS Employment WITH
    `the employee` IS `s 171ZU test person`
    `the kind of employer` IS `a company or other body corporate`
    `the employment began on` IS began
    `the employment ended on` IS ended
    `held under a contract of service` IS TRUE
    `held in an office` IS FALSE
    `carried on in Great Britain` IS TRUE

`s 171ZU test office holder` MEANS Employment WITH
    `the employee` IS `s 171ZU test person`
    `the kind of employer` IS `the Crown`
    `the employment began on` IS Date 1 1 2025
    `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING
    `held under a contract of service` IS FALSE
    `held in an office` IS TRUE
    `carried on in Great Britain` IS TRUE

`s 171ZU test neither` MEANS Employment WITH
    `the employee` IS `s 171ZU test person`
    `the kind of employer` IS `the Crown`
    `the employment began on` IS Date 1 1 2025
    `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING
    `held under a contract of service` IS FALSE
    `held in an office` IS FALSE
    `carried on in Great Britain` IS TRUE

`s 171ZU test abroad` MEANS Employment WITH
    `the employee` IS `s 171ZU test person`
    `the kind of employer` IS `a company or other body corporate`
    `the employment began on` IS Date 1 1 2025
    `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING
    `held under a contract of service` IS TRUE
    `held in an office` IS FALSE
    `carried on in Great Britain` IS FALSE

-- GENERATED by work/gen_zc.py.  Expected values follow from the text: every paragraph of the set must be satisfied.

§§ `s 171ZU(2) the conditions (claimant mother)`

-- Field order of `s 171ZU(2) the claimant mother's case`:
--    1. (a) the claimant mother and P satisfy prescribed conditions as to caring or intending to care for the child
--    2. (b)(i) P satisfies prescribed conditions as to employment or self-employment
--    3. (b)(ii) P satisfies prescribed conditions as to having earnings of a prescribed amount for a prescribed period
--    4. (b)(iii) P satisfies prescribed conditions as to relationship either with the child or with the claimant mother
--    5. (c) weeks of continuous employment ending with the prescribed week
--    6. (c) the prescribed length of continuous employment in weeks
--    7. (d) at the end of that prescribed week the claimant mother was entitled to be in that employment
--    8. (e) normal weekly earnings in pounds for the prescribed period ending with the prescribed week
--    9. (f) regulations so provide that the person continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time
--   10. (f) the claimant mother continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time
--   11. (g) the claimant mother became entitled to statutory maternity pay by reference to the birth of the child
--   12. (h) the claimant mother satisfies prescribed conditions as to the reduction of the duration of the maternity pay period
--   13. (i)(i) the claimant mother has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks she would be entitled to claim if the entitlement were fully exercised
--   14. (i)(ii) the claimant mother has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks she intends to claim
--   15. (i)(iii) the claimant mother has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks in respect of which P intends to claim
--   16. (j) the claimant mother has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the period or periods during which she intends to claim
--   17. (k)(i) a notice under paragraph (i) or (j) is given by such time as may be prescribed
--   18. (k)(ii) a notice under paragraph (i) or (j) satisfies prescribed conditions as to form and content
--   19. (l) P consents to the extent of the claimant mother's intended claim
--   20. (m) it is the claimant mother's intention to care for the child during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to her
--   21. (n) the claimant mother is absent from work during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to her
--   22. (o) the person is an employee within the meaning of the Employment Rights Act 1996
--   23. (o) the claimant mother's absence from work during each such week is absence on shared parental leave
