§§ `s 171ZZ4 supplementary`

-- (1) the three period definitions point at the other provisions' periods
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(1) adoption pay period` (`s 171ZU test period` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 28 1 2026)) EQUALS `s 171ZU test period` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 28 1 2026)
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(1) maternity allowance period` (`s 171ZU test period` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 4 2 2026)) EQUALS `s 171ZU test period` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 4 2 2026)
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(1) maternity pay period` (`s 171ZU test period` (Date 5 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026)) EQUALS `s 171ZU test period` (Date 5 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026)
-- (1) "local authority" and "local authority foster parent" mean what the Children Act 1989 says; the Act is outside the sources
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(1) the body is a local authority` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(1) the body is a local authority` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(1) the person is a local authority foster parent` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(1) the person is a local authority foster parent` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1) "employer": liable under s 6, or would be but for 6(1)(b) or the employee's being under 16
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(1) the person is the employer of the employee` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(1) the person is the employer of the employee` FALSE TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(1) the person is the employer of the employee` FALSE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- would be liable but for age, but s 173(a) says the employee is not under 16: no
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(1) the person is the employer of the employee` FALSE FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- would be liable but for age, and s 173(a) does not answer: not covered
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(1) the person is the employer of the employee` FALSE FALSE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- none of the limbs: "means a person who ..." says no
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(1) the person is the employer of the employee` FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(1) the person is the employer of the employee` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1) "modifications includes additions, omissions and amendments"
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(1) the change is a modification` `s 171ZZ4(1) an addition` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(1) the change is a modification` `s 171ZZ4(1) an omission` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(1) the change is a modification` `s 171ZZ4(1) an amendment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(1) the change is a modification` `s 171ZZ4(1) another kind of change` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1) "prescribed means prescribed by regulations"
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(1) the matter is prescribed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(1) the matter is prescribed` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2) "employee": in Great Britain, under a contract of service or in an office, with general earnings
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(2) the person is an employee` (`s 171ZU test employment` (Date 1 1 2025) NOTHING) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(2) the person is an employee` (`s 171ZU test employment` (Date 1 1 2025) NOTHING) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(2) the person is an employee` (`s 171ZU test office holder`) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(2) the person is an employee` (`s 171ZU test neither`) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(2) the person is an employee` (`s 171ZU test abroad`) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (5) week: Sunday-start unless regulations prescribe otherwise.  Wed 7 Jan 2026's week begins Sunday 4 Jan 2026.
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(5) the week convention` EQUALS `a period of 7 days beginning with Sunday or another prescribed period`
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(5) the first day of the week containing the day` (Date 7 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 4 1 2026)
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(5) the first day of the week containing the day` (Date 4 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 4 1 2026)
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(5) the first day of the week containing the day` (Date 3 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 28 12 2025)
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(5) the first day of the week containing the day` (Date 7 1 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6) average weekly earnings: 800 over 8 weeks is 100; a prescribed other calculation, or no weeks, is not covered
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(6) the person's normal weekly earnings in pounds` 800 8 FALSE EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(6) the person's normal weekly earnings in pounds` 800 8 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ4(6) the person's normal weekly earnings in pounds` 800 0 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
